silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_concrete_anchor#d_mittens_category silm:hasLongDescription "The D_Mittens_Category is D_Mittens_Category: the locally small category used as the instantiation of C in the Yoneda lemma statement; objects = twelve source nodes + MittensColimitApex; morphisms = the twelve typed legs plus identity arrows and compositions." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.00_whitepaper.chapters.07_yoneda_profile_drill.sections.02_yoneda_lemma_statement.concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensColimitApex is MittensColimitApex: the concrete instantiation of the object A in the Yoneda lemma; the colimit of D_Mittens; Mittens-the-individual-cat assembled from all twelve legs. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'A', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_concrete_anchor#clinicallabelpresheaf a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.00_whitepaper.chapters.07_yoneda_profile_drill.sections.02_yoneda_lemma_statement.concrete_anchor#clinicallabelpresheaf" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_concrete_anchor#clinicallabelpresheaf silm:hasLongDescription "The ClinicalLabelPresheaf is ClinicalLabelPresheaf: the concrete instantiation of the presheaf F; assigns to each D_Mittens source node X the set of clinical labels for X stored in VetRecord_77 or associated clinic systems. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
